---
import LegalLayout from '../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import {
	COOKIES_PATH,
	LEGAL_CONTACT_EMAIL,
	LICENSE_PATH,
	REFUNDS_PATH,
	SITE_BRAND,
	TERMS_PATH,
} from '../../lib/seo';
---

<LegalLayout
	title="Privacy Policy"
	description="How iStockVisual.com handles accounts, download logs, visual-search uploads, and on-device studio tools."
	heading="Privacy Policy"
	lede="We collect what we need to run accounts, serve the library, and operate visual search. Studio tools keep your files on your device."
>
	<h2>1. Who we are</h2>
	<p>
		This policy describes how {SITE_BRAND} (“we”) handles personal data when you visit
		istockvisual.com, create an account, download assets, use visual search, or open Help chat.
		Related rules: <a href={TERMS_PATH}>Terms of Use</a>, <a href={LICENSE_PATH}>Content License</a>,
		<a href={COOKIES_PATH}>Cookie Policy</a>, <a href={REFUNDS_PATH}>Refund Policy</a>.
	</p>
	<p>
		The Service is hosted on Cloudflare. Account and session records are stored in Cloudflare D1 (and
		session storage such as KV where used for sign-in). Library files and short-lived visual-search
		uploads are stored in Cloudflare R2.
	</p>

	<h2>2. Information we collect</h2>
	<h3>Account</h3>
	<p>
		When you sign up we store your name, email address, a hashed password, plan type (free or Pro),
		and plan expiry if applicable. We do not store your password in plain text.
	</p>
	<h3>Usage needed to run the Service</h3>
	<ul>
		<li>Session cookies so you stay signed in and so free vs Pro sizes apply</li>
		<li>
			Download requests (asset, size such as 512 / 1K / 2K / 4K / 8K) so we can enforce plans and
			the HD fair-use cap
		</li>
		<li>
			Standard request logs on our host (IP address, user agent, URL, and similar technical data)
			for security and abuse prevention
		</li>
	</ul>
	<h3>Visual search</h3>
	<p>
		If you search with a photo, that file is uploaded so we can match it against the library
		(including color). Query photos are stored under a visual-search prefix and are deleted after
		about one hour. They are not published in the library and are not used on this site to train a
		public model.
	</p>
	<h3>Help chat</h3>
	<p>
		The on-site assistant answers from a fixed support brief (license, plans, tools, privacy). Do
		not paste passwords or payment numbers into chat. We may keep short operational logs of abuse or
		errors; chat is not a substitute for emailing a refund request.
	</p>
	<h3>Information we do not collect from studio tools</h3>
	<p>
		Image Editor, Convert, Vectorizer, Social Resizer, Batch Watermark, and Palette Generator run
		locally in your browser. Those files — and extracted palettes — are not uploaded to iStockVisual.
		The same is true of the on-page editor when it works from a preview already on your device.
	</p>
	<h3>Theme preference</h3>
	<p>
		Light or dark theme is saved in your browser’s local storage (<code>istockvisual-theme</code>).
		That value does not leave your device.
	</p>
	<h3>Privacy notice</h3>
	<p>
		A short on-site notice may appear once every 24 hours per browser or IP address. Closing it
		stores a timestamp in a first-party cookie and local storage
		(<code>istockvisual-privacy-ok</code>), and a hashed IP key in our edge store so the same
		network is not prompted again that day. We do not keep the raw IP for this notice.
	</p>

	<h2>3. How we use information</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>Create and maintain your account</li>
		<li>Authenticate sessions and protect against scrape and credential abuse</li>
		<li>Provide free and paid downloads and enforce plan and fair-use limits</li>
		<li>Run visual search and then delete the query photo</li>
		<li>Respond to support, refund, or legal requests</li>
		<li>Keep the Service secure and available</li>
	</ul>
	<p>We do not sell your personal information.</p>

	<h2>4. Cookies and similar storage</h2>
	<p>
		We use essential cookies for sign-in and security. Theme preference uses local storage, not a
		cookie. Visual search may keep a short-lived query reference in session storage on your device.
		Details: <a href={COOKIES_PATH}>Cookie Policy</a>.
	</p>

	<h2>5. Sharing</h2>
	<p>
		We share data with infrastructure providers only as needed to host and operate the Service
		(currently Cloudflare for the Worker, D1, R2, and related edge features). We may disclose
		information if required by law, to protect the Service or other users, or in connection with a
		transfer of the Service to a successor operator, who must handle the data under comparable
		protections.
	</p>
	<p>
		Payment details, when checkout is completed through a processor, are handled by that processor —
		we do not intend to store full card numbers on iStockVisual.
	</p>

	<h2>6. Retention</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>
			Account data is kept while the account is open, and for a reasonable period afterward if needed
			for security, refunds, or legal records
		</li>
		<li>Visual-search query photos are removed after about one hour</li>
		<li>Download and server logs are retained only as long as needed for operations and abuse review</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>7. Your choices</h2>
	<p>
		You can update account details while signed in, sign out at any time, and control theme in the
		header. To correct data, close an account, or request a copy of the personal data we hold, email
		<a href={`mailto:${LEGAL_CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{LEGAL_CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> from the address on the
		account. We may need to verify the request.
	</p>
	<p>
		Depending on where you live, you may have rights to access, correct, delete, or restrict
		processing of your personal data, and to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority. We will
		honor requests required by applicable law.
	</p>

	<h2>8. International processing</h2>
	<p>
		Cloudflare may process data in more than one region. By using the Service you understand that
		your information may be processed outside the country where you live, with safeguards provided
		by our host.
	</p>

	<h2>9. Children</h2>
	<p>
		The Service is not directed at children under 16, and we do not knowingly collect personal data
		from them. If you believe a child has created an account, contact us and we will delete it.
	</p>

	<h2>10. Changes</h2>
	<p>
		We may update this policy. The “Last updated” date on this page is the effective date. Continued
		use after a change means you accept the revised policy.
	</p>

	<h2>11. Contact</h2>
	<p>
		Privacy questions: <a href={`mailto:${LEGAL_CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{LEGAL_CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
	</p>
</LegalLayout>
